import{_ as t,o as i,c as n,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const p=JSON.parse('{"title":"Developing Catch-up Civilization","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/35-发展中赶超型文明.md","filePath":"en/35-发展中赶超型文明.md","lastUpdated":1789183869000}'),a={name:"en/35-发展中赶超型文明.md"};function l(r,e,s,c,h,d){return i(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="developing-catch-up-civilization" tabindex="-1">Developing Catch-up Civilization <a class="header-anchor" href="#developing-catch-up-civilization" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Developing Catch-up Civilization&quot;">​</a></h1><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Content</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Document No.</td><td>35</td></tr><tr><td>Module</td><td>Civilization Typologies and Social Systems</td></tr><tr><td>Keywords</td><td>Developing Catch-up, Latecomer Advantage, Concentrated Breakthrough, Strategic Allocation, Leapfrog Development</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="i-origins-and-core-concepts-of-the-developing-catch-up-civilization" tabindex="-1">I. Origins and Core Concepts of the Developing Catch-up Civilization <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-origins-and-core-concepts-of-the-developing-catch-up-civilization" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Origins and Core Concepts of the Developing Catch-up Civilization&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Developing Catch-up Civilization is the most dynamic of the five symbiotic civilization typologies, with origins traceable to the development models of developing countries in the real world. These regions often have weak foundations, relatively scarce resources, and late development starts, but also possess huge development potential and strong development will. After the establishment of the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, drawing on the successful experiences of developing countries&#39; catch-up development, and combining with symbiotic concepts, the unique civilizational form of the &quot;Developing Catch-up Civilization&quot; was created.</p><p>The core concept of the Developing Catch-up Civilization can be summarized in eight characters: &quot;latecomer catch-up, concentrated breakthrough.&quot; Specifically:</p><ol><li><strong>Latecomer advantage</strong>: late-starting regions can avoid the detours and sunk costs of early development, directly learning from the mature experiences and advanced technologies of developed regions, achieving &quot;overtaking on curves&quot;</li><li><strong>Concentrated breakthrough</strong>: with limited resources, concentrating forces on key fields and key links, achieving breakthroughs at key points first, then driving overall development from point to area</li><li><strong>Learning and innovation</strong>: on the basis of learning from advanced experiences, combining one&#39;s own actual conditions for innovation, avoiding both &quot;closing the door&quot; and &quot;copying mechanically&quot;</li><li><strong>Gradual advance</strong>: formulating staged development goals, advancing step by step, maintaining strategic focus and strategic patience</li></ol><p>These concepts of the Developing Catch-up Civilization are highly compatible with the core concepts of the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization: &quot;self-growth through one&#39;s own way&quot; emphasizes that each civilization must find its own path, &quot;common progress of the Myriad Races&quot; emphasizes the common development of all regions, and &quot;A Path for Everyone&quot; emphasizes that every region and every individual has the right to development.</p><h2 id="ii-the-social-structure-of-the-developing-catch-up-civilization" tabindex="-1">II. The Social Structure of the Developing Catch-up Civilization <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-the-social-structure-of-the-developing-catch-up-civilization" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. The Social Structure of the Developing Catch-up Civilization&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The social structure of the Developing Catch-up Civilization takes &quot;strong government + strategic planning + mobilized society + open learning&quot; as its basic features:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Structural Element</th><th>Feature Description</th><th>Core Function</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Strong Government</td><td>The government has strong planning and mobilization capabilities, responsible for formulating and implementing development strategies</td><td>Concentrating resources, driving development</td></tr><tr><td>Strategic Planning</td><td>Formulating medium and long-term development plans, clarifying staged goals and key fields</td><td>Guiding development direction</td></tr><tr><td>Mobilized Society</td><td>Society has strong collective action capability, able to concentrate forces on major tasks</td><td>Supporting strategic implementation</td></tr><tr><td>Open Learning</td><td>Actively learning advanced experiences and technologies from other civilizations</td><td>Achieving rapid improvement</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="_2-1-strong-government" tabindex="-1">2.1 Strong Government <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-1-strong-government" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.1 Strong Government&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The government of the Developing Catch-up Civilization is a typical &quot;development-oriented government,&quot; with strong planning and mobilization capabilities:</p><ul><li><strong>Formulating development strategies</strong>: clarifying the civilization&#39;s development direction and strategic priorities</li><li><strong>Concentrating resources</strong>: concentrating limited resources on key fields through planning and coordination</li><li><strong>Organizing major projects</strong>: organizing large-scale infrastructure and major cultivation projects</li><li><strong>Providing public services</strong>: rapidly improving the level of public services such as education, medical care, and housing</li></ul><p>The core concept of the development-oriented government is &quot;government-driven development&quot; — in the early stages of development, the government plays the role of the &quot;locomotive&quot; of development, leading society forward.</p><h3 id="_2-2-strategic-planning" tabindex="-1">2.2 Strategic Planning <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-2-strategic-planning" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.2 Strategic Planning&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The Developing Catch-up Civilization places great importance on strategic planning, formulating development plans at multiple levels and in multiple time scales:</p><ul><li><strong>Long-term plans</strong>: planning the civilization&#39;s development direction and goals over decades</li><li><strong>Medium-term plans</strong>: clarifying the key tasks and goals of the next five to ten years</li><li><strong>Short-term plans</strong>: arranging annual development tasks and resource allocation</li></ul><p>The strategic planning system ensures the continuity and stability of development, avoiding the problem of &quot;changing the direction whenever leadership changes.&quot;</p><h3 id="_2-3-mobilized-society" tabindex="-1">2.3 Mobilized Society <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-3-mobilized-society" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.3 Mobilized Society&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The Developing Catch-up Civilization has strong social mobilization capability:</p><ul><li><strong>Collective action</strong>: society can quickly concentrate forces to accomplish major tasks</li><li><strong>National sentiment</strong>: citizens have strong identification with the nation and civilization, willing to contribute to development</li><li><strong>Sense of mission</strong>: citizens regard the civilization&#39;s development as their own mission, with a strong sense of responsibility</li></ul><p>This social mobilization capability enables the Developing Catch-up Civilization to achieve in a short time what developed civilizations take decades to accomplish.</p><h3 id="_2-4-open-learning" tabindex="-1">2.4 Open Learning <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-4-open-learning" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.4 Open Learning&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The Developing Catch-up Civilization emphasizes open learning, actively absorbing the advanced experiences and technologies of other civilizations:</p><ul><li><strong>Learning cultivation systems</strong>: introducing and digesting the Three Hundred Origin Cultivation Systems, improving them according to local conditions</li><li><strong>Learning management experience</strong>: learning the management models of developed civilizations, improving governance efficiency</li><li><strong>Introducing talents and technology</strong>: attracting talents and introducing technology from other civilizations to accelerate development</li></ul><p>Open learning enables the Developing Catch-up Civilization to achieve rapid improvement by standing on the shoulders of giants.</p><h2 id="iii-the-cultivation-model-of-the-developing-catch-up-civilization" tabindex="-1">III. The Cultivation Model of the Developing Catch-up Civilization <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-the-cultivation-model-of-the-developing-catch-up-civilization" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. The Cultivation Model of the Developing Catch-up Civilization&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The cultivation model of the Developing Catch-up Civilization takes &quot;elite-led, universal popularization, practical orientation&quot; as its core features:</p><h3 id="_3-1-elite-led" tabindex="-1">3.1 Elite-Led <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-1-elite-led" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.1 Elite-Led&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The Developing Catch-up Civilization first concentrates limited cultivation resources on cultivating a batch of elite talents:</p><ul><li><strong>Elite selection</strong>: selecting cultivators with the best talent and potential through rigorous screening</li><li><strong>Priority training</strong>: providing elite cultivators with priority resource support and high-quality mentors</li><li><strong>Breakthrough missions</strong>: elite cultivators undertake key technical research and cultivation breakthroughs</li></ul><p>The elite-led model enables the Developing Catch-up Civilization to form core competitiveness in key fields in a short time.</p><h3 id="_3-2-universal-popularization" tabindex="-1">3.2 Universal Popularization <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-2-universal-popularization" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.2 Universal Popularization&quot;">​</a></h3><p>While cultivating elites, the Developing Catch-up Civilization does not neglect universal cultivation:</p><ul><li><strong>Universal education</strong>: popularizing basic cultivation education, improving the cultivation level of the entire population</li><li><strong>Elite returning to society</strong>: elite cultivators give back to society through teaching, guidance, and technical services</li><li><strong>Gradual expansion</strong>: as resources grow, gradually expanding the scope of cultivation support</li></ul><p>The universal popularization model ensures the broad mass base of the civilization and continuously enriches the reserve of talents.</p><h3 id="_3-3-practical-orientation" tabindex="-1">3.3 Practical Orientation <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-3-practical-orientation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.3 Practical Orientation&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The cultivation model of the Developing Catch-up Civilization emphasizes practical orientation:</p><ul><li><strong>Problem-oriented</strong>: cultivation research and talent training centered on solving actual development problems</li><li><strong>Application priority</strong>: emphasizing the transformation of cultivation achievements into actual productive forces</li><li><strong>Practice testing</strong>: testing cultivation results in actual practice, rather than pursuing empty realms</li></ul><p>The practical orientation ensures the efficiency and pertinence of the cultivation model, avoiding waste of limited resources.</p><h2 id="iv-the-output-linked-contract-mechanism-of-the-developing-catch-up-civilization" tabindex="-1">IV. The Output-Linked Contract Mechanism of the Developing Catch-up Civilization <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-the-output-linked-contract-mechanism-of-the-developing-catch-up-civilization" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. The Output-Linked Contract Mechanism of the Developing Catch-up Civilization&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The output-linked contract mechanism of the Developing Catch-up Civilization takes &quot;strategic contracting&quot; as its main form:</p><ol><li><strong>Strategic tilt</strong>: resource allocation tilts toward key strategic fields and key projects, ensuring breakthroughs at key points</li><li><strong>Merit-based allocation</strong>: more resources are allocated to cultivators and teams with outstanding performance, encouraging competition</li><li><strong>Development support</strong>: providing development support to underdeveloped regions and groups, narrowing internal development gaps</li><li><strong>Gradual advance</strong>: reasonably planning the progress of resource allocation, avoiding one-time excessive concentration</li></ol><p>The advantage of this &quot;strategic contracting&quot; mechanism is its ability to concentrate resources on key fields, achieving rapid breakthroughs; it also needs to pay attention to balancing the relationship between key breakthroughs and comprehensive development.</p><h2 id="v-advantages-and-challenges-of-the-developing-catch-up-civilization" tabindex="-1">V. Advantages and Challenges of the Developing Catch-up Civilization <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-advantages-and-challenges-of-the-developing-catch-up-civilization" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Advantages and Challenges of the Developing Catch-up Civilization&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="_5-1-typical-advantages" tabindex="-1">5.1 Typical Advantages <a class="header-anchor" href="#_5-1-typical-advantages" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;5.1 Typical Advantages&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li><strong>Fast development</strong>: the strong government and social mobilization capability achieve rapid development</li><li><strong>Strong breakthrough capability</strong>: concentrated resource investment achieves breakthroughs in key fields</li><li><strong>Latecomer advantage</strong>: learning from mature experiences, avoiding detours and sunk costs</li><li><strong>Strong development will</strong>: the strong desire for catch-up provides sustained development momentum</li></ul><h3 id="_5-2-facing-challenges" tabindex="-1">5.2 Facing Challenges <a class="header-anchor" href="#_5-2-facing-challenges" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;5.2 Facing Challenges&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li><strong>Weak foundation</strong>: insufficient infrastructure, cultivation systems, and talent reserves</li><li><strong>Unbalanced development</strong>: regional and group development gaps may be large</li><li><strong>Sustainability pressure</strong>: high-intensity development may bring resource and environmental pressures</li><li><strong>Institutional maturity</strong>: institutions may not be mature enough, requiring continuous improvement</li></ul><p>In response to these challenges, the Developing Catch-up Civilization is actively absorbing the advantages of other typologies, such as introducing the social protection mechanism of the Nordic Welfare Type and the innovation incentive mechanism of the North American Pluralistic Type, achieving a balance between development speed and development quality.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Developing Catch-up Civilization is the most dynamic civilization typology of the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization. With the core concept of &quot;latecomer catch-up, concentrated breakthrough,&quot; it achieves rapid development and key breakthroughs through the social structure of strong government, strategic planning, mobilized society, and open learning, the elite-led universal popularization cultivation model, and the strategic contracting output-link mechanism. While maintaining its own characteristics, the Developing Catch-up Civilization is also continuously improving its institutional design, moving toward higher quality and more balanced development.</p><h2 id="related-documents" tabindex="-1">Related Documents <a class="header-anchor" href="#related-documents" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related Documents&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>30-五种共生文明分型总览 (Overview of the Five Symbiotic Civilization Typologies)</li><li>31-东亚集约型文明 (East Asian Intensive Civilization)</li><li>36-社会结构与阶层流动 (Social Structure and Class Mobility)</li></ul>',54)])])}const u=t(a,[["render",l]]);export{p as __pageData,u as default};
